flowchart TD
    Wake["<b>1. task becomes runnable</b><br/>wakeup, fork, or preemption<br/>makes a task eligible<br/><b>handoff:</b> sched_ext asks BPF<br/>where it should wait<br/><b>state:</b> task has runnable state<br/>and previous CPU"]

    Enq["<b>2. ops.enqueue</b><br/>BPF chooses DSQ, slice,<br/>FIFO or vtime ordering<br/><b>handoff:</b> task must wait<br/>until a CPU needs work<br/><b>state:</b> scx_bpf_dsq_insert*<br/>records queue ownership"]

    DSQ["<b>3. dispatch queue</b><br/>kernel-managed runnable-task<br/>queue ordered by policy<br/><b>handoff:</b> dispatch can move<br/>work to a CPU-local DSQ<br/><b>state:</b> task is queued,<br/>not yet running"]

    Dispatch["<b>4. ops.dispatch</b><br/>CPU needs work, BPF calls<br/>scx_bpf_dsq_move_to_local<br/>or inserts local work<br/><b>handoff:</b> core scheduler runs<br/>only from the local DSQ<br/><b>state:</b> selected task is<br/>local to that CPU"]

    Run["<b>5. CPU runs task</b><br/>task consumes slice until<br/>block, preempt, yield, or exit<br/><b>handoff:</b> runnable again means<br/>another enqueue cycle<br/><b>state:</b> runtime accounted,<br/>watchdog sees progress"]

    Wake --> Enq --> DSQ --> Dispatch --> Run
    Run -. blocks then wakes / slice ends .-> Wake

    classDef bpf fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#d97706,stroke-width:2px
    classDef state fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    classDef run fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb,stroke-width:2px
    class Enq,Dispatch bpf
    class Wake,DSQ state
    class Run run
